          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "8.1 Multiplication of Fractions"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.332,
            0.516,
            0.369
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Aaron walks 3 kilometres in 1 hour. How far can he walk in 5 hours?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.369,
            0.517,
            0.444
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "This is a simple question. We know that to find the distance, we need to find the product of 5 and 3, i.e., we multiply 5 and 3."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.447,
            0.499,
            0.467
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Distance covered in 1 hour = 3 km."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.472,
            0.262,
            0.491
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Therefore,"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.496,
            0.433,
            0.516
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Distance covered in 5 hours"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.28,
            0.525,
            0.388,
            0.545
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_0_equation_9.jpg",
          "content": "= 5 \\times 3    km"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.23,
            0.561,
            0.438,
            0.58
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_0_equation_10.jpg",
          "content": "3+3+3+3+3 \\mathrm{km}"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.524,
            0.366,
            0.819,
            0.568
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 11,
              "bbox": [
                0.524,
                0.366,
                0.819,
                0.568
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_0_image_11.jpg",
              "content": ""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.453,
            0.598,
            0.543,
            0.616
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "= 15 km."
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.64,
            0.851,
            0.681
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "？ Aaron’s pet tortoise walks at a much slower pace. It can walk only "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\frac { 1 } { 4 }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " kilometre in 1 hour. How far can it walk in 3 hours?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.69,
            0.848,
            0.748
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Here, the distance covered in an hour is a fraction. This does not matter. The total distance covered is calculated in the same way, as multiplication."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 15,
          "bbox": [
            0.291,
            0.757,
            0.707,
            0.858
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 15,
              "bbox": [
                0.291,
                0.757,
                0.707,
                0.858
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_0_image_15.jpg",
              "content": ""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 16,
          "bbox": [
            0.175,
            0.892,
            0.52,
            0.92
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Distance covered in 1 hour "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "= { \\frac { 1 } { 4 } }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " km."
            }
          ]
